# Copy to mobile/business/.env — gitignored, never committed.

# Same value the website's VITE_API_URL points at, but ABSOLUTE: the app has
# no dev-server proxy to resolve a relative path against. Use the versioned
# prefix (/api/v1), not the website's /api — see api's next.config.ts rewrite.
#   Local:  http://192.168.1.X:3000/api/v1  (your machine's LAN IP, not
#           localhost — Expo Go runs on the PHONE, which can't reach your
#           computer's loopback address)
#   Prod:   https://alassema.com/api/v1
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=""

# Origin that serves root-relative media ("/img/seed-15.jpg" — project photos,
# offering images). Leave BLANK in production: the deploy is single-origin
# (deploy/Caddyfile). Local dev is the exception — see mobile/client's own
# .env.example for the full explanation; the LAN IP it names is the same one
# to point this at here.
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_ASSET_URL="http://192.168.1.X:5173"
EXPO_PUBLIC_ASSET_URL=""

# Optional shared gate matching the website's VITE_API_KEY / the backend's
# API_KEY (api/.env.example). Unset on the server today, so this does
# nothing either way — but if API_KEY is ever set there, every request from
# this app needs the matching X-Api-Key header or it 401s (see api's
# proxy.ts). Leave blank unless the server side is also configured.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY=""

# No Google/Apple/Turnstile keys here on purpose. Staff sign in with email
# and password only (POST /auth/login) — this app offers no third-party
# sign-in and no public-facing form that needs a CAPTCHA.

# Sentry DSN (phase 13 — hardening). Leave BLANK to leave crash reporting off
# entirely — @alassema/mobile-shared's initErrorReporting() no-ops until this
# is set, no network call is made either way. Events are scrubbed before
# transport (no tokens/passwords/phone numbers/financial figures — see
# errorReporting.ts) and tagged with role + app version.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=""
